      "content": "that makes sense, but the shareholders are still really skeptical. they keep saying that any money spent on 'social' or 'environmental' stuff that doesn't have a direct, immediate ROI is basically just a breach of fiduciary duty. can you give me some specific arguments that support their view? i want to make sure i'm being fair to their perspective before i pivot to the ESG side.",
